            <ArticleTitle>Ancillary role of vitamin C in pink aesthetics.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2014-208559</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2014208559</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A smile expresses feelings of joy, affection and self-confidence in an individual. Melanin hyperpigmentation of the gingiva jeopardises the aesthetics of an individual significantly. In the present case, gingival depigmentation was performed with a surgical scalpel along with local applications of ascorbic acid, yielding satisfactory aesthetic results with low subjective pain levels, and no recurrence has been observed after 9 months of follow-up.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>2015 BMJ Publishing Group Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
